  "_comment": "Multidimensional structured-scene schema for the Victorian chemical-works case. Hartwick Chemical Works, an unnamed northern industrial city, winter (February) 1889. A Board of Trade factory inspector (Henry Gould) is killed on the canal path beside the sulphur storage; the works manager Silas Oake used the unlit canal-bend rather than direct force. The red herring is James Whitlow, a compensated worker whose grievance is real and whose behaviour is suspicious but whose role is the opposite of suppression. Universal core dimensions shared with amber_cipher / hollow_season / third_signature; case-specific extension INDUSTRIAL_TELL covers the chemical / log-revision / sulphur-trace observables that are the precise physical evidence of the case (the maintenance log entries overwritten in slightly different ink and slightly different hand; the three-day gap; the shoe-print and button at the canal bend; the smell of sulphur on a coat that was meant to have stayed home). Tokens listed in anchor_tokens are graph/convergence anchors only — never emitted directly.",

